Item 5: harness fidelity (Chris)

Uncommitted on top of 9e30961cdbe5 (series head, pushed); item5.diff = `git diff` (harness only,
tools/asahi/g15-pb-growth-tests.py).

FINDING (Chris)
(1) The harness's Pools::drop_chunks() resets the ledger at once (ledger.reinit()), while
production reclaim_check() frees the chunks and defers the reset to the next render's InitBM,
so freed_chunks_are_mapped_again ran from a state production never has. (2) The harness
extracted neither reclaim_check() nor reclaim_delay_ns(). (3) Wanted: the actual reclaim/free
and scheduling bodies, the old posted count kept until InitBM, a same-client render after
60 ms and after 1.1 s, a compute-only submission between the reclaim and the InitBM; mutations
still caught.

VALIDATION OF THE FINDING
- (2) is already fixed by item 3 (reclaim_check(), free_backing(), note_idle(),
  reclaim_delay_ns(), free_chunks() and the reclaim params run actual since b375d3d2/34653844).
- (1) and (3) real at 9e30961c: a production mutant that resets the posted count at the idle
  reclaim instead of at the InitBM (`reinit-at-idle-reclaim`: `self.pools.ledger.reinit();`
  before free_backing() in the idle path) SURVIVES the current harness: "33 passed; 0 failed",
  failed: [] (M3 ~/Projects/build-out/kernel-stack177/i5pre/). drop_chunks() is still used by
  freed_chunks_are_mapped_again (twice).

FIX (harness only)
- Pools::drop_chunks() removed from the model.
- New helper publish(f, vm, render): as engine.rs: map_pb() first (before the flight is
  added), then for a render prefix with reinit pending the InitBM (reset_ledger(), i.e. the
  actual Pools::init() ledger-reset statements the harness already checks) and reinit cleared;
  then the flight is added with its renders flag and the idle noted.
- New helper defaults(): resets the five parameter cells; called at the start of every
  parameter-setting test (supervisor's item 4 nit).
- freed_chunks_are_mapped_again rewritten on the actual reclaim: A grows to 1100 posted
  (above the floor, below half the maximum), retires and leaves the registry, the idle reclaim
  at 1 s frees to 2 chunks without walking A (posted kept: "posted count reset before the
  InitBM"), B's first render re-inits (posted 64) and grows the backing again with new
  objects, A's next publication replaces its stale aliases (chunks-2 unmaps and maps), a
  second idle reclaim walks B and A's aliases past the backing go at its next catch-up.
- same_client_render_after_60ms: 2100 posted, idle 60 ms: reinit + reclaim_pending set,
  posted and chunks unchanged; the same VM renders: InitBM -> posted 64, flags cleared; grows
  back to 2100 with NO backing event (no alloc/map/unmap/free) and every record within the
  mapped blocks.
- same_client_render_after_1_1s, for 1500 (idle reclaim at 1 s) and 2100 (client boundary at
  50 ms, then the free at 1 s): checks at 0, 50 ms, 1 s, 1.1 s; 2 chunks left, posted kept,
  the VM's aliases cut to 2; the same VM renders: InitBM; grows back with every chunk backed and
  mapped before a record/producer names it (assert_posted_backed from 2 chunks).
- compute_between_reclaim_and_initbm: 1500 posted, level-2 reclaim at 1 s; a compute-only
  prefix of the same VM is published and a growth request naming its ctx is queued; 4 passes:
  no alloc/map/unmap/free/record/producer/reply, reinit still pending, posted still 1500, the
  request counted bad (left unanswered); the compute retires, a later check does nothing, the
  next render re-inits and grows over fresh chunks mapped before they are posted.
- Mutations: reinit-at-idle-reclaim (same_client_render_after_1_1s, "posted count reset
  before the InitBM (1500)"), reinit-at-any-reclaim (same_client_render_after_60ms, "posted
  count reset before the InitBM").
- Docstring bullet.

FIX VALIDATION (M3 chroot, ~/Projects/build-out/kernel-stack177/i5/)
- pb-growth --mutations: "36 passed; 0 failed"; 36 mutations, 36 caught by their intended
